 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? The quickest and easiest way is with your shoes on. Sit on the seat, barefoot, and ask a friend stand the seat to you. If your legs feel short or the tops of your legs start to burn, the seat is too short. Push down on the lever and slide the seat forwards. That's help you sit on the seat without your feet on the ground, and you can adjust the length from there. Lower the seat as far as the post will go, and add a short length of tube to the post. You can find them for bikes at a bike shop. You should only barely touch it. Too much is as bad as too little.",
